something that can speak is anything with:
    a way to speak.
    a way to greet with name (text), giving back text.
a speaker is anything with:
    a way to speak.
    a way to speak.
a dog is a kind of thing with:
    name, which is text.
a fish is a kind of thing with:
    name, which is text.
a cat is a kind of thing with:
    name, which is text.
to speak, for a dog:
    say "woof".
to greet, for a dog, with name (text), giving back text:
    give back "hi " followed by name.
to speak, for a cat:
    say "meow".
to greet, for a cat, with name (a number), giving back text:
    give back "hi".
let zoo be an empty list of things that can speak.
add (a new fish with name "Nemo") to the end of zoo.
add (a new cat with name "Tom") to the end of zoo.
let pet be item 1 of zoo.
say pet's name.
say jump with pet.
say greet pet with 5.
say speak pet.
say greet pet.
let mixed be a list of (a new dog with name "Rex") and (a new cat with name "Tom").
if 1 is 1:
    a thing is anything with:
        a way to speak.
let maybe pet be the first item of zoo.
a mixer is anything with:
    a way to mix with x (text) and y (text), giving back text.
to try with blender (a mixer):
    say mix blender with "a".
